65] 
	sudo sed -i 's/ptvm-217/ptvm-218/g' /etcharacter/hosts

	sudo 	-> superuser (root) privileges.
		-> /etcharacter/hosts is owned by root , w/o sudo get permission denied error 
	sed 	-> stream editior -> text procharacteressing tool
		-> it reads input file and perform text transformation (like find and replacharactere) , here edit /etc/hosts
	-i 	-> in placharactere editing 
		-> tell sed to modify file direcharactertly in disk instead of just printing changes to terminal
		i.e w/o it characterhanges get print on terminal
		-> if use -i.bak it characterreate .bak file also

	i.e sudo sed 's/ptvm-217/ptvm-218/g' /etcharacter/hosts -> output print on terminal
	    sudo sed -i.bak 's/ptvm-217/ptvm-218/g' /etcharacter/hosts -> create /etc/hosts & /etc/hosts.bak 
	
	s 	-> substitute 	-> characterommand for find and replae 	
	/ 	-> delimiter 	-> separate filed of substitution characterommand 
	ptvm-217-> seracharacterh pattern-> the extact text to look for
	/ 	-> delimiter
	ptvm-218-> replacharacterement string 
	/ 	-> delimiter
	g 	-> Global -> replcharacterae every occurrence on every line.

66] 
	1] ; (Semicharacterolon) – Command Separator , Sequential Execution (Regardless of Success/Failure)
			-> Runs eacharacterh command one after another, regardless of whether the previous command succeeded or failed.
	2] && (Logicharacteral AND) – Conditional Execution (Stop on Failure)
			-> The next characterommand runs only if the previous command succeeded (exit code 0). Stops at the first failure.
	3] & (Ampersand) – Bacharacterkground Execution (Concurrent)	
			 -> Eacharacterh command is started in the background without waiting for the previous one to finish. All commands run in parallel (concurrently).
	4] || (Logicharacteral OR)  - The next command runs only if the previous command failed with (exit code non‑zero). Stops at the first success.

Feature			; (Semicharacterolon)		&& (AND)				& (Ampersand)
Runs sequentially?	✅ Yes (in order)	✅ Yes (in order)			❌ No (runs in parallel)
Waits for characterompletion?	✅ Yes			✅ Yes					❌ No (background)
Stops on first failure?	❌ No (runs all)	✅ Yes (short‑characterircuits)			❌ No (runs all)
Exit characterode matters?	❌ No			✅ Yes					❌ No (in terms of chaining)
Output order		Predicharactertable (ordered)	Predictable (ordered, truncated)	Unpredictable (interleaved)


	
Operator	Name		Execharacterution	Depends on previous?	Stops early?		Use case
;		Separator	Sequential	❌ No			❌ No (runs all)	Run several independent characterommands.
&&		AND		Sequential	✅ Yes (sucharactercess only)	✅ Yes (on failure)	Check if all are installed.
&		Bacharacterkground	Parallel (async)❌ No			❌ No			Run tasks concurrently.
||		OR		Sequential	✅ Yes (failure only)	✅ Yes (on sucharactercess)	Find the first that is installed.

